  This is a dependency audit of the current written suppliers, informed by
  the independent chapter reviews in this folder. It is not an assertion that
  every line of the source manuscripts has been independently reconstructed
  in this last pass.

  <section|Finite lattice and ultraviolet
  chain><label|finite-lattice-and-ultraviolet-chain>

  1\U4 specify the actual group/trace normalization, observables and
  original-law reflection positivity, fixed local sections, exact normalized
  block kernel and representation dictionaries. Random frame choices are
  retained in full read regions.

  5 supplies the actual rooted predictor derivative, quadratic identities,
  stationary branch and fixed-scale free-horizon convergence. Its path/metric
  hypotheses are supplied by the propagated path classes in7/9, with10
  selecting their finite stage floors; they are structural hypotheses of
  local estimates, not a remaining independent existence assumption.

  6 supplies the same-law selected energy, extracted affine-square
  correction, primitive local factors and joint tails.7 identifies the
  weighted stationary/classical and one-loop path outputs.8 supplies cited
  connected-expansion results with explicit smallness.9 retains exact actual
  density reconstruction and the local stationary remainder.10's parameter
  and coupled-cutoff estimates apply to that same coefficient construction;11
  carries full higher marked modes, and12 uses the full graph and fixed-rung
  comparison for the full ultraviolet limit. No new unsupported quantitative
  supplier was identified in the current dependency trace; previous audit
  corrections concerned actual tree/gauge identification, normalization,
  support reserves and affine-square extraction and are recorded in their
  respective reviews.

  <section|Field quotient and finite detectors><label|field-quotient-and-finite-detectors>

  The equation-adapted microscopic identity in2 is exact against every
  external spectator.11 compares that fixed section with the same-history
  physical section, retaining factor-scaling conjugation and the
  square-root-allowance payment. Its common polynomial extraction, retimed
  actual restarted history, covariance comparison and finite-arity marker
  restoration provide the detector rows before continuum extraction. The
  normalized-null and moving-complement argument therefore apply in13 without
  selecting an independent equation plane.13's sharp bounds, derivative
  calculus and repeated-word estimates precede the later phase construction.

  The new bounded coarse residual supplier is now proved with a full source
  polynomial and exact pullback-discrepancy identity. It has the correct
  physical degree factors, polynomial attachment heights and recovered
  support reserve at every adjacent step. Its scalar unit part is treated
  separately. The bounded real approximation is consequently available
  for15's variance argument without an additional hypothesis.

  <section|Local replacement and Ward identities><label|local-replacement-and-ward-identities>

  The graded quotient and lattice grouped-product estimates are inserted
  in13. They use the actual11 signed local transport and all-copy rooted
  norms,13 sharp weights and the corrected physical quotient. Their mixed
  local replacement has no phase or Ward premise. Hence14's annular
  cancellation follows with rho^(1\<minus\>epsilon) before any rotation or
  phase conclusions.14's finite-menu free comparison uses one actual T and
  one longest restarted window, restricted for its different magnifications.
  The coordinate spectral/mixed-sign/diagonal/angular argument has been
  independently audited and the temporal-gap, growing-width and signed-dyadic
  details corrected. Thus the Ward/rotation construction no longer requires a
  bare annular or free-comparison supplier assumption.

  <section|Exact all-copy supplier for phase
  nondegeneracy><label|exact-all-copy-supplier-for-phase-nondegeneracy>

  Use11 <verbatim|ch11:n-mark-comparison> with <strong|two marks per replica
  cell>. Its R1 and R2 equal15's displayed corrected singleton and pair
  errors (the pair constant is ss'\<minus\>c). At fixed comparison depth k
  their root bound is B_k=H_k^(-1/32), uniform in the total replica census.
  Take simultaneous bounded label limits at that fixed k along the already
  selected correlation refinement. For each fixed integer j, the chessboard
  bound on 2j translated corrected copies is B_k^(2j); the constants precede
  j, though the cutoff/translation tails may depend on j. The
  repeated-word/cluster identity15:cluster then yields the moment
  inequality15:detector-moments. Taking deeper k makes gamma_k tend to zero.
  This does not rerun the finite-arity construction at arity2j and therefore
  does not introduce uncontrolled j-dependent constants. The injective free
  detector rows imply every phase has the same null space. This supplier
  paragraph has been inserted in15.

  15's bounded variance approximation now cites the proved13 supplier. Its
  phase symmetry, same fields, almost-everywhere ground line and uniform
  slabs feed16.16's tied-gap locality has the explicit fixed-boost
  neighborhood, and its subsequent uniform low-energy argument handles
  exceptional phases; neither is inferred from a phase-dependent bound.

  <section|Assembly recommendation><label|assembly-recommendation>

  Within this audited dependency graph, no substantive unproved
  <em|additional> supplier remains in groups1\U3 of the assembly theorem.
  They can be replaced by references to the established constructions,
  keeping the original fixed-data/local-lemma hypotheses and finite-stage
  choice order. Residual wording such as16's 'outstanding microscopic
  hypotheses' and15's former 'Suppose' should be updated rather than read as
  a new assumption. The current-transfer/radius-comparison trace asymptotic
  of17 remains a separate review task; this audit makes no recommendation on
  removing its assumptions. Contact normalization choices remain separate
  from existence and from positivity at collisions.

  Final integration note: Chapter17 subsequently supplied the
  current-transfer rates and variable-stage comparison, with independent
  reviews in ch17-score-independent-review.md and
  chapter-17-spatial-moments-review.md. Chapter19 now states the trace
  corollary without an additional unproved transfer hypothesis. Its core
  construction/OPE dependency chain is unchanged.
